{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:16DecisionDiagrams06BinaryA7DiagramV","title":"BinaryDecisionDiagram","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram.swift#L27","fileName":"BinaryDecisionDiagram.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"DecisionDiagrams"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram"}],"role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryDecisionDiagram"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Variables are tested in index order, 0 nearest the root. The table never holds two vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that test the same variable with the same children, nor a vertex whose children are equal, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each function has one vertex: two "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Function","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" values are equal exactly when they are the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)          \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)              \/\/ 5","diagram.vertexCount(of: f)                            \/\/ 5: x0, x1, x2 and both constants","let g = diagram.restrict(f, variable: 2, to: false)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1","g == diagram.and(x0, x1)                              \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Functions are built by the mutating methods, which add vertices to the table and leave every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"existing function as it was; a function belongs to the table it was built in and its copies."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The table keeps every vertex it has made."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A shared table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams: Boolean functions of a fixed number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of variables, each a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test one variable and branch to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"low child (the variable false) and a high child (true), down to the constants (Bryant,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“Graph-Based Algorithms for Boolean Function Manipulation”, 1986)."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/ComputedTableStatistics-swift.struct","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Function","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/GraphView-swift.struct","doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Operator"],"generated":true,"anchor"